{
  "requirement": "Before drafting, the `habeas-requirements` skill MUST direct agents to ask the user whether uncommitted edits to the book that the agent did not make in the current task belong to the task.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The requirement has one obligation. Before drafting, the `habeas-requirements` skill must direct agents to ask the user whether uncommitted book edits that the agent did not make in the current task belong to the task.\n\nThe marked test `tests/authoring_cli.rs#fn[the_requirements_skill_asks_about_foreign_edits_before_drafting]` covers it:\n- It finds the workflow step containing \"If it has uncommitted edits you did not make in this task, ask the user whether they belong to it\". `step_of` panics if no step contains that phrase, so a skill that drops the ask fails the test. The skill's step 1 contains it.\n- It asserts that this step also contains \"Run `git status` on the book's source directory\". That ties the check to uncommitted edits in the book, which is the requirement's \"to the book\" scope.\n- It asserts `ask < step_of(SKILL, \"Write drafts\")`, which enforces \"before drafting\". The skill's step 1 is the ask and step 2 is the draft.\n\nThe skill text asks the user, in the skill's own wording, whether the edits belong to the task. The test pins that phrase, so it covers the \"ask the user whether they belong\" clause. The requirement states no further conditions, modes or failure cases. No acknowledgments apply.",
